{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793390358,"nonce":"Hos2yhiFphv3EsqDNjiuD0ebYh4=","message":"ashui landed the OpenFL Graphics parity items on its local main (not pushed; details and limits in ashui git-bug fb2e74e): fills (4988d50, 8ab05e0: Brush.placed, spreading and focused gradients, Brush.bitmapPattern with matrix, repeat, smooth), blend modes Normal/Add/Subtract/Multiply/Screen and colour transforms with offsets in 0..1 (0f6b1ba: divide OpenFL offsets by 255), non-nesting masks via pushMask/popMask (10b8471), stroke scale modes and hairlines and drawPath (d75831e), drawTriangles and drawQuads without edge antialiasing (5490179), PixelSurface.bitmap() as a brush or image source and image9 for scale9Grid (6ae4cbc). scrollRect maps to pushClipRect; cacheAsBitmap needs nothing. Not built: overlay, hardlight, difference, invert, darken, lighten, layer, alpha, erase (they read the target), nested masks and a live surface brush (ashui f3c4c86); text untouched. For the replay tier: this covers the shape, fill, transform, blend and mask core; filters, shaders and text stay on the pixel-surface path. Separately, RayDE does not compile against ashui main since 4988d50 (see next comment).","files":null}]}